# Component structure

- Prefer small, focused components. When a file grows large (hundreds of lines), extract subcomponents, hooks, or helpers into colocated files in the same folder.
- Keep the default export readable: orchestration at the top level, details in named subcomponents or `use*` hooks.
- Reuse shared UI from workspace packages (e.g. `@wisihe/ui-react`) before duplicating markup.

## React Compiler

This repo uses the **React Compiler**. Do **not** add manual memoization in app code: avoid `useMemo`, `useCallback`, and `memo` / `React.memo` unless the user explicitly asks or there is a documented exception. Write straightforward components and hooks; let the compiler optimize. Details: root `AI_RULES.md`.

See canonical patterns in existing sections under `apps/*/app/components/` or `apps/*/src/components/`.
